{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3659","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3659","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3659\",\"parent_revision\":\"26840bd9f526369138d5ab94099ac91ee24d6d345fd595d9e2f193eda72783bb\",\"root_revision\":\"26840bd9f526369138d5ab94099ac91ee24d6d345fd595d9e2f193eda72783bb\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P1\\ntype: Bug\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-09-19\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nTwo defects in the `pattern:` mechanism that `work/feasibility-gate.md` Criterion 3 uses.\\n\\n1. The impact-analyst writes `pattern:` annotations that `agents/impact-analyst.md:299-302` forbids (\\\"A grep pattern must precisely enumerate the scope; if it cannot, omit `pattern:`\\\"), and nothing checks them before the gate runs. On #3060 (Impact Radius 7.3) it annotated an out-of-scope agent-files row with `pattern: 'summary=False'` and a documentation row with `pattern: '#3060'`. #3060 changes two strings and one description in one file; no row enumerates a sweep.\\n\\n2. The gate compares `rg -l '<pattern>' | wc -l` (a count of files) with the \\\"manually-authored row count\\\" (a count of Systems Inventory rows), per `feasibility-gate.md` and the worked example at `impact-analyst.md:306-318`. A row can name a directory (`src/api/`), so the two numbers count different things. In the spec's own example the gate can report 30 files against 2 rows and emit STALE_GROOM on the day of grooming.\\n\\nObserved: `rg -l 'summary=False' plugins/development-harness | wc -l` returned 21 against a 5-file row (ratio 4.2x), and the gate stopped #3060's work stage with STALE_GROOM. The item's scope had not grown.\\n\\nImpact: the gate blocks items whose scope has not changed, and it cannot detect the scope growth it exists to detect, because the comparison does not measure growth since grooming.\\n\\nExpected: the gate stops an item only when the files a sweep must touch have grown since grooming.\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Session observation, work stage of #3060, 2026-09-20\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-09-19\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"4b3d7eb790607e236a88b5725d60028f764ebf08cbe5d6c99f9f397bb3267283\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABVoHpOA\"}"}